# Both variables are OPTIONAL. Leave them unset to use same-origin requests:
# - In local development, the Vite dev server proxies /api and /ws to the
#   backend (see vite.config.ts, target controlled by VITE_BACKEND_TARGET
#   which defaults to http://localhost:8080 and is only read by Vite itself,
#   never bundled into client code).
# - In production, the frontend is expected to be served from the same origin
#   as the backend (e.g. behind the project's nginx reverse proxy), so relative
#   /api and /ws paths resolve correctly without any configuration.
#
# Only set these if the frontend is deployed on a different origin than the
# backend. Remember: any VITE_ variable is bundled into the client build and is
# publicly visible, so never put secrets here.

# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com
# VITE_WS_URL=wss://api.example.com/ws
